    <string name="health_atlas_motion_signal">The nerve signals</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_motion_signal_caption">Motor nerve endings release acetylcholine, exciting the muscle fiber membrane.</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_motion_calcium">Calcium is released</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_motion_calcium_caption">Excitation travels down a T-tubule, triggering calcium release from the sarcoplasmic reticulum into the muscle fiber.</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_motion_slide">Filaments slide</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_motion_slide_caption">Calcium enables the filaments to interact. Actin slides past myosin; the sarcomere shortens while the individual filaments keep their lengths.</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_motion_pull">Tendon pulls the forearm</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_motion_pull_caption">The biceps contracts, transmitting tension through its tendon to the radius, and the forearm rises around the elbow.</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_motion_release">Relaxation and extension</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_motion_release_caption">Calcium returns to storage and the biceps relaxes. The triceps contracts and pulls on the ulna to extend the elbow.</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_bone_sense">Osteocytes sense change</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_bone_sense_caption">Osteocytes embedded in bone sense changes in loading or local damage and help regulate remodeling.</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_bone_remove">Osteoclasts remove old bone</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_bone_remove_caption">Multinucleated osteoclasts attach to the bone surface and break down mineral and organic matrix, leaving a resorption pit.</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_bone_prepare">Preparing the surface</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_bone_prepare_caption">Cells on the bone surface help clear the resorbed area and prepare for formation. Resorption and preparation can overlap at nearby sites.</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_bone_fill">Osteoblasts lay new matrix</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_bone_fill_caption">Osteoblasts secrete unmineralized matrix, called osteoid, gradually filling the local pit.</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_bone_mineral">The new matrix mineralizes</string>
    <string name="health_atlas_bone_mineral_caption">New matrix gradually mineralizes. Some osteoblasts become embedded in the matrix as osteocytes.</string>
